      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In theory, one could argue that staying home is a moral act of \"voting with one's feet\" by rejecting a corrupt system you agree to leave, as silence is sometimes a powerful form of dissent against tyranny. However, in a local democracy where a lack of voters is often the one power used to maintain the very status quo you oppose, that argument dissolves into selfishness. Ultimately, even a principled boycott fails to create any alternative reality, while casting a vote—however imperfect—remains the only genuine attempt to force change.",
      "source": "target",
